<title>UK: Parity gets British Telecom contract.</title>
<headline>Parity gets British Telecom contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Information services group Parity Plc said on Wednesday it received a contract from British Telecommunications Plc to develop its Customer Call Behavioural Analysis technology.</p>
<p>&quot;This is a high profile, strategic, new technology development as CCBA is reputed to be the largest Oracle Data Warehouse in Europe currently in live operation,&quot; Parity said in a statement.</p>
<p>The size of the contract was not disclosed.</p>
<p>Parity's shares jumped 15p to 317-1/2p in morning trade.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
